Vision Statement:
Aim High - Achieve your full potential
Mission Statement:
At Sellincourt School, we are committed to respecting and valuing the rights of others and encouraging self-belief. We promote consideration, compassion, honesty, and trust whilst developing responsible and independent learners. We have high expectations of our children and are committed to each child reaching their full potential.
Values:
Respect - to encourage children's respect and tolerance for human rights, as well as respect for their parents and the environment;
Equality - to foster a regard for justice and equality, to be considerate and act in a responsible manner;
Trust/Honesty - to earn and build trust so that we can work and learn co-operatively, share ideas but be individuals together;
Responsibility - to encourage children to understand that in order for people to have rights, we have responsibilities to ensure that we do not harm others or ourselves and that we take responsibility for our actions;
Kindness - to treat others with compassion.

